Suppress noisy "Did not detect DSR response" warning from defaults.lua.

This is a false positive when running nvim inside tmux: nvim sends OSC 11
+ DSR and waits up to 100ms for the DSR reply. tmux and kitty both support
DSR, but the 100ms wait is sometimes exceeded during heavy plugin-load
startup, producing the warning on every nvim launch.

Upstream fix lands in nvim master via PR #38699 (merged 2026-04-24), which
adds an `NVIM_NOTTYFAST=1` env var and a `'nottyfast'` option to disable
the bg-detection block entirely. That PR is NOT in 0.12.1.

  - PR:    https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/38699
  - Issue: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/38648

Remove this overlay once nixpkgs ships a neovim containing commit 66149ca6
(or any later 0.12.x patch release). At that point set
`home.sessionVariables.NVIM_NOTTYFAST = "1"` instead.

--- a/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua
+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/_core/defaults.lua
@@ -982,9 +982,6 @@
         -- Don't show the warning when running tests to avoid flakiness.
         and os.getenv('NVIM_TEST') == nil
       then
-        vim.notify(
-          'defaults.lua: Did not detect DSR response from terminal. This results in a slower startup time.',
-          vim.log.levels.WARN
-        )
+        -- silenced via overlay; see overlays/neovim-suppress-dsr-warning.patch
       end
     end

